MCP TOOLS, COMMAND LIMITS AND ERROR CLASSIFICATION

DEFAULT SERVER
  mcpd &                temperature-only MCP service
  mcpd --shell &        enable shell/manual/file tools
Shell mode has no authentication or TLS. Use trusted isolated LAN.

TOOLS
  get_temperature()        read RP2040 onboard temperature
  get_manual()             return index
  get_manual({topic: ...})  read one ROM manual page
  execute_command({command: ...})  run short shell command
  write_file({path: '/tmp/name', content: ASCII_TEXT})
Read actual tools/list schema; do not assume an argument name.

MCP-EXECUTABLE TASK SEQUENCE
  get_manual()
  get_manual({topic:'languages/python'})
  write_file({path:'/tmp/test.py',content:'print(42)\n'})
  execute_command({command:'python /tmp/test.py'})
  execute_command({command:'ps'})

LIMITS
  command string must fit the 119-character server command limit;
  output <=4096 bytes; command wait ~3000 ms.
  write_file maximum RAM file 2048 bytes; ASCII input only.
  Six process slots; shell and command consume task slots.
  Long-running full-screen and interactive tools are unsuitable.

HTTP CHUNKED ERROR
  'incomplete chunked read' means HTTP response ended too early;
  it does not prove the executed command did or did not run.
  After reconnecting, inspect ps and target state, then retry a
  read-only bounded command. Do NOT blindly retry state changes.

AGENT INSTRUCTIONS
  Prefer help, ls, cat /man and short finite commands.
  Preserve user files; do not call rm/kill/device writes unless asked.
  Report exact tool output and distinguish errors from conjecture.
